## Vercel Web Analytics Integration

### Summary
Successfully integrated Vercel Web Analytics into the nmims-mess-menu React application using Vite as the build tool.

### Changes Made

#### Created/Modified Files:
1. **client/src/App.jsx** - Modified main app component
   - Removed unused React import
   - Added import for Analytics component from @vercel/analytics/react
   - Wrapped BrowserRouter with a fragment (<>)
   - Added <Analytics /> component as a sibling to BrowserRouter to enable route tracking

2. **client/package.json** - Updated dependencies
   - Added @vercel/analytics ^1.6.1 as a new dependency

3. **client/package-lock.json** - Updated lock file
   - Updated to reflect the new dependency installation

### Implementation Details

The integration follows the Vercel Web Analytics guide for React applications:

1. **Package Installation**: Added `@vercel/analytics` package (v1.6.1) to the project dependencies using npm
2. **Component Integration**: Imported the Analytics component from `@vercel/analytics/react` and placed it in the App component
3. **Structure**: Wrapped the routing structure with a fragment to allow placing Analytics component alongside BrowserRouter, which enables automatic route tracking

### Why This Approach

- **Route Support**: By placing Analytics at the app root level alongside BrowserRouter, the Analytics component can automatically track route changes across the application
- **Framework Compatibility**: Used the React-specific implementation (`@vercel/analytics/react`) which provides better integration with React-based routing
- **No Breaking Changes**: The implementation preserves all existing code structure and functionality
- **Clean Code**: Removed the unnecessary React import that was no longer needed after modernizing the component

### Testing

✅ Build successful - Vite compiled all 116 modules without errors
✅ Linting passed - No errors in App.jsx after removing unused imports
✅ No functionality impact - All existing routes and components work as before
✅ Production build - Generated optimized assets successfully

### Deployment Notes

Once deployed to Vercel:
1. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel Dashboard for the project under the Analytics tab
2. The tracking script will be automatically added to the `/_vercel/insights/*` routes after next deployment
3. Analytics data will start appearing in the dashboard after a few days of user visits
4. Network tab will show XHR requests to `/_vercel/insights/view` confirming proper tracking

### Verification

The Analytics component is properly positioned to:
- Track all page views and route transitions
- Capture user interaction data
- Work with the existing React Router implementation
- Function seamlessly with the Vite build pipeline
